er, flowback and well testing, water containment, fluids hauling, water monitoring, and water network automation; AquaView automation services; technology solutions comprising hydrographic mapping, water volume and quality monitoring, remote pit and tank monitoring, leak detection, asset and fuel tracking, and automated-equipment services; and various surface rental equipment and workforce accommodation services. The Chemical Technologies segment offers technical solutions, products, and services related to chemical applications in the oil and gas industry; and water treatment and flow assurance solutions. This segment also develops, manufactures, manages logistics, and provides chemicals, including polymers for use in hydraulic fracturing, stimulation, cementing, and well completions; and offers production chemical solutions for underperforming wells, corrosion and scale monitoring, chemical inventory management, well failure analysis, and lab services. It serves oil and gas producers. The company was formerly known as Select Energy Services, Inc. and changed its name to Select Water Solutions, Inc. in May 2023. Select Water Solutions, Inc. was founded in 2008 and is headquartered in Gainesville, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John D. Schmitz | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $426K ranks in the bottom quartile among Energy peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Select Water Solutions, Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $2.5B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +0% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $80M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 14% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $112.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-112230862.92},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Energy peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Select Water Solutions Inc (WTTR) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record EBITDA, Pilot ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/select-water-solutions-inc-wttr-230139945.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794524499.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Select Water Solutions (WTTR): Rising Water Volumes and Long-Term Contracts Support Infrastructure Expansion","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/select-water-solutions-wttr-rising-175021531.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794505821.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.93,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Select Water Solutions (WTTR) Posts Strong Q3 Results, Is The Stock Still Cheap?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-wttr/select-water-solutions/news/select-water-solutions-wttr-posts-strong-q3-results-is-the-s","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794483083.673,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.966,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Citigroup Issues Pessimistic Forecast for Select Water Solutions (NYSE:WTTR) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/citigroup-issues-pessimistic-forecast-for-select-water-solutions-nysewttr-stock-price.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794424726.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.273,"tier":0,"scope":"comp